       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/tq268fs9721.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Pencil, treble edge, at the tail of the roll. Five figures, very faint and cut along their tops by the crop edge. The last is the barred 7 of these hands and the one before it a 2, giving the year 27; the middle figure matches the 5 of the roll number written at the head of the roll (crop 3), giving May; the fourth-from-last is a 2, so the day ends in 2, but its first figure is illegible and I have not guessed it. Crop 4 shows the printed leader label, WELTE-MIGNON No. 3045, Debussy Preludes, M. Welte & Soehne Freiburg i. B., with a signature in the \"Played by\" box; it carries no date. Crop 2 is a damp stain."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
